            <ArticleTitle>Organ-specific regulatory T cells of thymic origin are expanded in murine prostate tumors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e24898</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Little is known about the relative contributions of self-specific regulatory T cells (Tregs) of thymic origin and induced Tregs generated extrathymically to the pool of tumor-infiltrating Tregs. We have recently demonstrated that thymic-derived Tregs reactive to a prostate-associated self antigen are highly and recurrently enriched within oncogene-driven murine prostate cancers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
